{"title":"Gas — Gas — daily — today","description":"Today's U.S. gas price averages about $4.36 per gallon for regular on October 8, 2026. This gasoline price update compares today's national average with yesterday, last week, last month and a year ago, explaining why a small weekly decline does not mean your fuel budget has recovered. Next, we cover mid-grade at $4.88 and premium at $5.27 per gallon, followed by an audience question about fuel costs. We finish with diesel at $6.28, last year's premium comparison and the regular-gas record from June 2022. Figures come from the supplied AAA daily averages and are rounded to the nearest cent for presentation. What are you paying for regular in your\n\nFor entertainment and informational purposes only. This is not financial, legal, medical, or other professional advice. Consult a qualified professional about your circumstances. We are not responsible for decisions or results based on this video.\n\n#gaspricestoday #USgasprices #nationalaveragegasprice #AAAgasprices #regulargasolineprice","tags":["gas prices today","US gas prices","national average gas price","AAA gas prices","regular gasoline price","premium gas prices","diesel prices today","gas prices October 2026","gas prices year over year","gasoline price comparison"],"fallback_query":"American gas station fuel pumps","frame":"classic","frame_color":"#ffffff","voice_id":"iP95p4xoKVk53GoZ742B","voice_gender":"male","music_mood":"light rhythmic instrumental groove, warm keys, crisp soft percussion, curious and approachable, steady moderate energy, no ominous tension, no sirens or trailer impacts","sfx":true,"voice_provider":"elevenlabs","audio_provider":"elevenlabs","reporter_on":false,"hook":"Regular gas averages about $4.36 per gallon nationwide today, above last year's $3.12.","reporter_prompt":"Five-second opening with a middle-aged American male reporter wearing a gray henley, standing beside regular gasoline pumps at an American gas station. Actual fuel dispensers and customers fueling vehicles remain visible behind him in soft daylight. Warm, conversational, confident delivery; no dramatic anchor performance. Horizontal composition. Use licensed real American stock footage throughout the subsequent edit. Apply the Inflation Economist design consistently: charcoal panels, orange numb","scenes":[{"text":"Regular gas averages $4.36 per gallon nationwide today, down slightly this week but above last year's $3.12—so drivers still pay more than a year ago.","query":"gas station American pumps","subject":"gas station","visual":{"type":"price_readout","headline":"gas station","prices":{"kind":"gas","metrics":[{"value":"$4.36","unit":"per gallon","period":"TODAY"}]}},"clip":{"url":"https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2015/08/09/175-135788388_large.mp4","kind":"video","author":"Republica (Pixabay)"},"clips":[{"url":"https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2015/08/09/175-135788388_large.mp4","kind":"video","author":"Republica (Pixabay)"}],"presentationOnly":false},{"text":"That's more money for the same fuel. So, is the recent dip actually easing your fuel budget?","query":"fueling driver American station","subject":"fueling driver","visual":{"type":"title","headline":"IS THE DIP ENOUGH?","sub":"The same fuel costs more","color":"dark"},"clip":{"url":"https://pixabay.com/get/gdd1f8339781a44a0b067d45615fadcf008e8201d27a0b60228a980f8352a3e271751faaa2ad4dbb8f7b859d305b7b63fe8901d04e43184e5233fa920d1adcda9_1280.jpg","kind":"photo","author":"Engin_Akyurt (Pixabay)"},"clips":[{"url":"https://pixabay.com/get/gdd1f8339781a44a0b067d45615fadcf008e8201d27a0b60228a980f8352a3e271751faaa2ad4dbb8f7b859d305b7b63fe8901d04e43184e5233fa920d1adcda9_1280.jpg","kind":"photo","author":"Engin_Akyurt (Pixabay)"},{"url":"https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2021/03/09/67364-522626695_large.mp4","kind":"video","author":"ChristianBodhi (Pixabay)"}],"presentationOnly":false},{"text":"First, that price is a national average for regular, not a promise about your neighborhood pump.","