esentationOnly":false},{"text":"That matters when your commute stays the same. Your weekly driving still needs fuel.","query":"commuter driving American highway","subject":"commuter driving","visual":{"type":"title","headline":"SAME COMMUTE, FUEL STILL NEEDED","sub":"A weekly budget expense","color":"dark"},"clip":{"url":"https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2020/10/28/53582-475000650_large.mp4","kind":"video","author":"dlabiebrzy (Pixabay)"},"clips":[{"url":"https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2020/10/28/53582-475000650_large.mp4","kind":"video","author":"dlabiebrzy (Pixabay)"},{"url":"https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2020/04/07/35266-407130741_large.mp4","kind":"video","author":"VReel (Pixabay)"}],"presentationOnly":false},{"text":"And regular isn't the only number to watch. The grade you buy changes your bill.","query":"grade selector American pump","subject":"grade selector","visual":{"type":"title","headline":"YOUR FUEL GRADE MATTERS","sub":"Different grades, different prices","color":"dark"},"clip":{"url":"https://pixabay.com/get/g7018ad5857787c53e8e91412bcb92feb4abfffe1c55dfb9891fe86da693b36783cce358733c27219706a84ef6efbe4ebf34efce203cf87a7e790766867bca010_1280.jpg","kind":"photo","author":"IADE-Michoko (Pixabay)"},"clips":[{"url":"https://pixabay.com/get/g7018ad5857787c53e8e91412bcb92feb4abfffe1c55dfb9891fe86da693b36783cce358733c27219706a84ef6efbe4ebf34efce203cf87a7e790766867bca010_1280.jpg","kind":"photo","author":"IADE-Michoko (Pixabay)"},{"url":"https://pixabay.com/get/g34f6805b3b5e85a68355dd981c8910d801942d48e399ffb3f42206f70505d2105a05771858139de9e69f5f9b6b980e7b72ed73eb4289855093a2d02ecec29975_1280.png","kind":"photo","author":"Emslichter (Pixabay)"}],"presentationOnly":false},{"text":"Mid-grade averages about $4.88 per gallon nationwide today.","query":"midgrade pump American station","subject":"midgrade pump","visual":{"type":"stat","headline":"U.S. MID-GRADE AVERAGE","sub":"per gallon • Oct. 8, 2026","value":"$4.88","color":"dark"},"clip":{"url":"https://pixabay.co